To terminate a C program, you can use the following methods:

1. Return 0 from the main function: This is the most common way to terminate a C program. When you return 0 from the main function, it indicates that the program executed successfully and terminates the program.

```c
int main() {
    // Your program code here
    return 0;
}
```

2. Use the exit() function: The exit() function is used to terminate the program immediately. It takes an integer argument that represents the exit status of the program.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your program code here
    exit(0);
}
```

3. Use the return statement with no value: If you use the return statement without specifying any value, it automatically returns 0 and terminates the program.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your program code here
    return;
}
```

